KG42.register("rules-0b1e2f0843340fefa127a01d",{"id":"05-double_auction::v141-c-R022","paper":"05-double_auction","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R022","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M04","name":"Counterparty matching","process_stage":"matching","market_meaning":"TR limits trading counterparties to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers; buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate. Scope: Trade Reduction auction; selection of buyers and sellers permitted to trade.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function matching.counterparties under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["matching.counterparties"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"Trade Reduction auction; selection of buyers and sellers permitted to trade.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R022-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"TR limits trading counterparties to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers; buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate. Scope: Trade Reduction auction; selection of buyers and sellers permitted to trade.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","location":{"location_id":"src-22913ad574-p03-c1r2__v141-a-M04-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1","anchor_text":"of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to 1 Ta buyers and sellers [45]. Suc","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The Trade Reduction (TR) auction mechanism avoids subsidization of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers [45]. Such differs from uniform k-DA and VCG, where $\\gamma$ buyers and sellers are allowed to transact. Because buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate in the TR auction, social welfare is not maximized. However, trading buyers pay $B_{\\gamma}^P$ and trading sellers receive $S_{\\gamma}^P$. As $B_{\\gamma}^P \\geq S_{\\gamma}^P$, the market operator may financially gain $B_{\\gamma}^P - S_{\\gamma}^P$ from each single unit transaction."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This rule declares no design/operational decision objects. The TR counterparty-selection outcome (which buyers/sellers trade) is determined by the mechanism rather than chosen as an optimization variable, and the frozen graph declares no variable object for it. The symbol $\\gamma$ appears in the source only as the marginal/breakeven index of the ordered offers (defined in the Section 2.1 uniform k-DA/VCG discussion), not as an optimization variable, and it is not declared here.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed constants/parameters are declared in the frozen R022 graph. The source's selection count uses the index $\\gamma$, but $\\gamma$ is a per-interval marginal/breakeven index defined by the natural ordering and breakeven condition elsewhere in Section 2.1; its definition is not contained in this rule's evidence v141-b-g01-ev-08, so it cannot be grounded as a parameter here without cross-scope reuse. No parameter object is therefore created."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M04-clearing","v141-a-M04-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"matching.counterparties","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","quote":"The Trade Reduction (TR) auction mechanism avoids subsidization of trades while maintaining truthful bidding by limiting trades to $\\gamma - 1$ buyers and sellers [45]."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-08","quote":"buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted to participate in the TR auction"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"3ca09bd189ab0131034f970e110cd3bd4207765c35f5b1b73ed7080319a9c5a2","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"R022 governs the TR auction's selection of counterparties (which buyers/sellers are permitted to trade). The source states a selection rule with an explicit count and exclusion: trades are limited to $-\\gamma - 1$ pairs, and the marginal buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$ are not permitted. This is a mathematical/selection object rather than a purely qualitative admission rule. However, the frozen R022 graph is V = {matching.counterparties}, E = [], x = [], theta = []: it declares no object for the marginal/breakeven index $\\gamma$, no ordered buyer/seller index sets, and no edge relating matching.counterparties to the selection/exclusion it performs. Expressing the rule faithfully would require those indices/sets and a selection member, none of which exist here, and their definition (largest breakeven index under the natural ordering rule) lies in the Section 2.1 uniform k-DA/VCG discussion rather than in this rule's own evidence v141-b-g01-ev-08. Per the frozen-graph rule, this math is therefore not invented; it is requested from C.1. C001 is preserved unchanged as a procedural, not_formalized statement. All B evidence (v141-b-g01-ev-08) remains UNREVIEWED in this experiment and is used only as candidate support, not as verified fact.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":["C.1: declare the marginal/breakeven index $\\gamma$ for R022 with explicit source scope, together with its defining condition under the natural ordering rule (largest breakeven index at which $B_{\\gamma}^{P} \\geq S_{\\gamma}^{P}$), because the R022 graph currently has no object for it and the source selection rule uses $\\gamma$ and $\\gamma - 1$.","C.1: declare the ordered buyer and seller index sets (bids sorted descending, asks sorted ascending) needed to express the permitted set {1, ..., $\\gamma - 1$} and the exclusion of buyer $\\gamma$ and seller $\\gamma$; these enumeration indices/sets are not in the frozen graph.","C.1: declare the selection/set member that the matching.counterparties function produces (the permitted counterparties) and an edge from matching.counterparties to that member (E is currently empty), so the selection/exclusion can be bound without inventing edges.","C.1: supply same-mechanism (v141-a-M04) evidence that defines $\\gamma$ within the TR scope, since v141-b-g01-ev-08 uses $\\gamma$ but its definition appears in the uniform k-DA/VCG text; this keeps the symbol source-scoped rather than cross-rule reused.","Reviewer note (experiment policy): v141-b-g01-ev-08 is UNREVIEWED candidate support; no claim is made that B transcription or this rule's science has passed independent source review."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
